From: Value Fabric Security Team <security@valuefabric.io>
Date: 2026-05-27
Subject: [PATCH-004] HIGH: Add PII Encryption Mixin for Layer 4 Agents

This patch introduces a SQLAlchemy mixin that provides transparent
application-level encryption for PII fields at rest.  It integrates
with the existing value_fabric.shared.crypto.EncryptedString type
and adds blind-index support for exact-match queries without
exposing plaintext.

Fields encrypted by default:
  - email        (with blind index for login/lookup queries)
  - phone        (with blind index for deduplication)
  - ssn          (encrypted only, no index — too sensitive)
  - address_line1 (encrypted only)
  - bank_account (encrypted only)

Key rotation is supported via the ENCRYPTION_KEY_VERSION env var.
When the key version changes, existing records continue to decrypt
(legacy ciphertext is detected and returned as-is), but new writes
use the current key.  A background re-encryption job can be run to
roll forward.

Security Impact: HIGH
Audit Ticket: SEC-2026-004
